Z||000000||Shiner||11-08-1999||02:34 AM||||If we really DON'T have emissions in my part of PA anymore...  I may accidentally leave the test pipe on in place of the cat.  How do you think my GT would sound with no cat and a flowmaster muffler?  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||11-08-1999||03:04 AM||||My friend had a GT without a cat and it was pretty loud. It was annoying after a while of riding in it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||11-08-1999||09:59 AM||||FM 2 chamber, too loud. Turbo, ok but a bit rumbly.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||11-08-1999||11:07 AM||||My 85 GT has a stock muffler with no cat, I think it sounds nice. Slightly louder, lower throaty sound. I like it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||11-08-1999||02:23 PM||||85 Duck-mobile. No converter, stock v6 GT muffler. Sounds great!||||reg||14
Z||000005||kornholio||11-08-1999||04:58 PM||||I bought the car not knowing that the previous owner got rid of the cat.  This thing is loud (V6)!  It has the stock muffler.  How much quieter can it get if I put a cat convertor back on?  It's not loud at all when I'm sitting in the car, though.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mutfish||11-08-1999||05:37 PM||||I ran a test pipe on my 88 gt for a short while after the converter failed....I didn't like the sound,too harsh.I bought a so called "high flow" catco converter and with the stock muffler, I think it sounds good...deep rumble at idle...quite at cruise speed.||||reg||1
Z||000007||superXmotorsports||11-08-1999||11:30 PM||||I think I have run different Fieros with every combo.  No cat, with stock system.  Straight pipes w/ cat.  Sprint headers and straight pipes (your neighbors LOVE you).  Borla XR1 no cat (nice low rumble for you quiet guys)  And finally the Ocelot system  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> bad resonantion at 3-4k RPMs.  I like the louder setups personally.  My next beast has full length headers and 4" (yes) pipes.  I'll keep you all posted.  By the way you can see the Borla and the straight pipes w/ 4.5" megs on my website: <A HREF="http://users.desupernet.net/superx" TARGET=_blank>http://users.desupernet.net/superx</A> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||Standard||11-09-1999||12:19 AM||||Has anybody tried the Gorlic stock exhaust system for the Duke?  The Fiero Store has the for $89.95, which seems like a really good price considering I was told $60 bucks for a muffler alone, and the Gorlic looks like cat-back and it comes with chrome tips...  I need to replace my muffler soon.  It's louder than those magnum v8's with the duel 3" tips...  Then again, I think it sounds kind of good at full throttle, but I'm sure the neighbors hate me...||||reg||5
Z||000009||DXR_DAD||11-11-1999||02:35 AM||||superX  That's one nice lookin ride!! can you post some pics of the exhaust system here? Even some off the car would be nice.<P>You have a real nice web page. I like your style!!||||reg||1
